Against Alexbeav/psxrecomp @ 94ea3b28 (release/wave2-v0.3.0-source), the exact
commit parasite-eve-recomp pins. Real `git diff` output, not hand-reconstructed.

Adds `fromfile_prefix_chars='@'` to compile_overlays.py's argument parser, so
a curated `--force-interior` address list can be passed as `@somefile` instead
of hundreds of repeated `--force-interior 0x...` arguments on one command
line. See findings/framework-findings.md finding #2 and build/play.ps1's
`-ForceInterior` handling for what this is for.

This is a workaround for a build-tooling ergonomics gap, not a fix for any
of the framework bugs in findings/ -- it doesn't change what gets compiled,
only how you tell the tool what to compile.

